From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] lwis: port to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(lwis: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx))

Port private/google-modules/lwis to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - iommu_register_device_fault_handler() removed (6.8): use the pixel_iommu fault registry that samsung_iommu.ko exports

Files: platform/busan/lwis_platform_busan.c

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * i3c: struct i3c_priv_xfer -> struct i3c_xfer and
    i3c_device_do_priv_xfers(dev, x, n) -> i3c_device_do_xfers(dev, x, n,
    I3C_SDR), as upstream renamed them (SDR is what priv xfers were).
---
diff --git a/lwis_fence.c b/lwis_fence.c
index 61a53c1..d014d75 100644
--- a/lwis_fence.c
+++ b/lwis_fence.c
@@ -78,7 +78,9 @@ int lwis_dma_fence_signal_with_status(struct dma_fence *fence, int errno)
 {
 	if (errno != 0)
 		dma_fence_set_error(fence, errno);
-	return dma_fence_signal(fence);
+	/* android-mainline: dma_fence_signal() returns void now */
+	dma_fence_signal(fence);
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static const char *lwis_fence_get_driver_name(struct dma_fence *fence)
